# Objective 2 — Tamil Nadu
#
# Policy: push everything — code, docs, images, data, ANSYS cases and the
# archive — EXCEPT files git cannot take. GitHub warns above 50 MB per file
# and rejects above 100 MB, so only the oversized files below are excluded.

# ── files over 50 MB (git cannot take these) ─────────────────────────────
# Measured, not guessed:
#   archive/openfoam_legacy/openfoam_case/run.log   223 MB  (past the 100 MB hard reject)
#   data/objective1/suntimes.csv                     80 MB  (past the 100 MB hard reject)
#   data/objective1/daily_aggregates_tamilnadu.csv   62 MB
#   ...and the archived copies of the same two files.
# All regenerate: suntimes.csv and daily_aggregates from Objective 1's
# 00b_build_suntimes.py and 02b_build_daily_aggregates.py; run.log is solver output.
**/suntimes.csv
**/daily_aggregates_tamilnadu.csv
**/openfoam_case/run.log

# Safety net for anything that grows past the limit later.
*.pkl

# ── never useful in git ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
tools/node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- superseded work, kept on disk but mostly out of git ---------------
# archive/ is retired material: the pre-restructure implementation, the
# OpenFOAM legacy tree, superseded ANSYS cases and voided results. Nothing in
# it is live and nothing was deleted -- it stays on disk for the record.
#
# REVISED 2026-11-10. Excluding archive/ wholesale was wrong in one specific
# way: 79 of the 373 path references in the checked documents resolve ONLY
# inside archive/, so `python scripts/g12_verify_docs.py` passed on the author's
# machine and would have reported 79 missing paths on a fresh clone. Those
# references are to retired DOCUMENTS and SCRIPTS, not to the heavy data.
#
# So: archive's text content is tracked (157 files, 1.2 MB) and its bulk is
# not (713 MB -- a 223 MB OpenFOAM run.log, 185 MB of CSVs, 117 MB of
# interactive HTML, 85 MB of JSON, the 63/81 MB Objective-1 aggregates).
# `archive/**` rather than `archive/` is deliberate: git does not descend into
# an excluded DIRECTORY, so the negations below would never be reached.
archive/**
!archive/**/
!archive/**/*.md
!archive/**/*.py
!archive/**/*.yaml
!archive/**/*.yml
!archive/**/*.rst
!archive/**/*.txt
# ...except the logs, which are .txt-adjacent bulk and regenerable.
archive/**/*.log
archive/**/run.log
